2026-10-22T04:55:00Z  VERIFY   The new test anEncryptedBodyBecomesAudio drives the whole path with no network: the encrypted selection, the key request, the streaming decrypt, and the extension. It asserts the file that lands is the plaintext, byte for byte, under an .m4a name.
2026-10-22T05:20:00Z  VERIFY   The C++ implementation against LIVE server data, not a fixture: the real rights response (HTTP 200, an anonymous request) and the real body head (HTTP 206 from the CloudFront media host) were unwrapped and decrypted with this project's own code -- unwrapped key 2001d3ad2262d52aaf9d542552ece3d8, counter 42c4e33256c76560f665ab5a7acddcbd, decrypted head 0000001c6674797069736f6d00000200, container MP4 (audio/mp4). The same values the browser-side capture produced, byte for byte.
